<%# ── In-page help drawer (#880) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    A quick lookup should not cost a context switch. This slides the contextual
    guide over the current screen, leaving the part-filled form visible beneath
    it, while #870's new tab stays one click away for anyone who wants to read
    the whole guide.

    First offcanvas in the app. It needs no new dependency (the Bootstrap 5.3.3
    bundle is already loaded in <head>) and no CSP change: the content is
    fetched same-origin into a Turbo Frame, so there is no frame-src and no
    connect-src to widen.

    Rendered once per page, at the end of <body>, outside the region Turbo
    replaces — help_drawer_controller tears it down on turbo:before-render. %>
<div class="offcanvas offcanvas-end sparc-help-drawer"
     id="sparc-help-drawer"
     tabindex="-1"
     aria-labelledby="sparc-help-drawer-title"
     data-help-drawer-target="drawer">

  <div class="offcanvas-header sparc-help-drawer-header">
    <h2 class="offcanvas-title h6 mb-0" id="sparc-help-drawer-title">Help</h2>

    <%# ms-auto is load-bearing. Bootstrap's offcanvas header is a plain flex
        row with NO justify-content — it right-aligns the close button purely
        via `.btn-close { margin-left: auto }`. Wrapping the close button in
        this group takes that auto-margin out of the header's own flex context,
        so without ms-auto both children bunch against the left edge with zero
        gap and the title sits jammed under the button. Caught by looking at
        the rendered screen; every test still passed. %>
    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 ms-auto">
      <%# The escape hatch #880 asks to keep prominent. Its href is repointed at
          whichever guide the drawer is showing, so "open the whole thing" is
          never a different page than the one being read. %>
      <%= link_to help_path,
            class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary sparc-help-drawer-full",
            target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer",
            data: { help_drawer_target: "fullGuide" } do %>
        Open full guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
      <% end %>

      <button type="button" class="btn-close"
              data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas"
              aria-label="Close help"></button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offcanvas-body sparc-help-drawer-body">
    <%# The frame starts with no src; the controller sets it on first open, so
        no page pays for a guide fetch nobody asked for. %>
    <%= turbo_frame_tag "help_drawer", data: { help_drawer_target: "frame" } do %>
      <p class="text-secondary mb-0">Loading the guide&hellip;</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
